# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Transient ---
*.tmp
*.log
logs/

# Generated demo artifacts. Three are committed exceptions: each is small, regenerates
# byte-identically, and is useful to a reader who will not clone and run anything.
#
# The two label-packet files are committed for a further reason. They are the exact artefact the
# owner's hold-out labels will be formed against, and a label is a judgement about a specific set
# of facts — so the facts have to be recoverable later, from the repository, at the digest the
# labels declare. An uncommitted packet would make the import's fingerprint check unfalsifiable.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/m2-demo.html
!artifacts/human-label-packet.xlsx
!artifacts/human-label-packet.jsonl

# The chaos suite's per-cell observations (M4.5). Working state: the run writes them, the renderer
# reads them, and the reviewed artefact is the table they produce in README.md. Committing them
# would make the same numbers exist in two places, and the copy nobody regenerates is the one a
# reader would trust.
.chaos-observations/
